= Semantic MediaWiki =

'''Semantic MediaWiki''' (SMW) is a MediaWiki extension that allows wiki pages to store typed semantic properties and relationships and query those annotations as structured data.

Instead of treating links and prose as the only machine-readable connections between pages, SMW can represent assertions such as a page's type, domain, provenance state, dependency, implementation relationship, or other explicitly defined property.

== Structured relationships ==

* Depends on: [[Depends on::MediaWiki]]

The relation identifies MediaWiki as SMW's host platform without implying that every MediaWiki installation uses SMW.

== Core capabilities ==

SMW provides property definitions, typed annotations, semantic queries, browsing/inspection surfaces, concepts as reusable query sets, and subobjects for structured facts that require identity below the page level.

The existence of a semantic edge does not prove the claim represented by that edge. Meaning, provenance, evidence, direction, and inference rules remain modeling responsibilities.

== Semantic MediaWiki in BITwiki ==

BITwiki uses SMW as the durable semantic graph/property layer. Canonical knowledge remains authored in MediaWiki pages, while stable structured facts and relationships are asserted through documented properties.

Scribunto/Lua is intended to operate above this state as a deterministic transformation and projection layer: normalize relationships, type-check contracts, derive safe display forms, generate contextual navigation, and expose diagnostics without replacing SMW as the state owner.

Native structured Lua access to SMW is provided by the separate SemanticScribunto integration (`mw.smw`) and must be treated as a deployment capability rather than assumed from SMW+Scribunto alone.

[[BIThub]] integrations can consume semantic views through explicit MediaWiki integration surfaces so the Discourse layer does not need to maintain an independent copy of BITwiki's knowledge graph.

